*Description of problem:*

etcd WAL fdatasync P99 latency increased by ~30% on OCP 5.0 FIPS enabled clusters after the RHCOS10 switch in {{5.0.0-0.nightly-2026-06-14-105938}}  which upgraded the kernel from from version 5.14 to 6.12:

!https://files.cornea.dev/api/public/dl/ee4GGGmh?inline=true|width=250!



We confirmed the regression is related to the kernel bump by a kernel downgrade experiment in [https://github.com/openshift/release/pull/81336|https://github.com/openshift/release/pull/81336] which restored latency to previous levels:

[https://gcsweb-ci.apps.ci.l2s4.p1.openshiftapps.com/gcs/test-platform-results/pr-logs/pull/openshift_release/81336/rehearse-81336-periodic-ci-openshift-eng-ocp-qe-perfscale-ci-main-aws-5.0-nightly-x86-control-plane-fips-24nodes/2072383118748160000/artifacts/control-plane-fips-24nodes/openshift-qe-orion-cluster-density/artifacts/output_cluster-density-v2_viz.html|https://gcsweb-ci.apps.ci.l2s4.p1.openshiftapps.com/gcs/test-platform-results/pr-logs/pull/openshift_release/81336/rehearse-81336-periodic-ci-openshift-eng-ocp-qe-perfscale-ci-main-aws-5.0-nightly-x86-control-plane-fips-24nodes/2072383118748160000/artifacts/control-plane-fips-24nodes/openshift-qe-orion-cluster-density/artifacts/output_cluster-density-v2_viz.html]

the osImage override was built with 5.0.0-0.nightly-2026-06-29-195240 rhel-coreos-10 overlay and kernel-5.14.0-687.15.1.el9_8

*Version-Release number of selected component (if applicable):*

{noformat}Starting with 5.0.0-0.nightly-2026-06-14-105938{noformat}

*How reproducible:*

{noformat}Always{noformat}

*Steps to Reproduce:*

{noformat}1. Install 24 nodes FIPS enabled cluster
2. Run perfscale CI control-plane workloads (cluster-density-v2, node-density, node-density-cni, crd-scale) using kube-burner
3. Measure etcd WAL fdatasync P99 latency via histogram_quantile(0.99, rate(etcd_disk_wal_fsync_duration_seconds_bucket[2m])){noformat}

*Actual results:*

{noformat}Significant increase after the switch to RHCOS10{noformat}

*Expected results:*

{noformat}etcd WAL fdatasync P99 latency on RHEL 10 (kernel 6.12) should be within 10% of RHEL 9 (kernel 5.14) levels. Current delta is ~30%, well above the 10% tolerance.{noformat}

*Additional info:*

{noformat}{noformat}

